{{!< default}}
{{!-- The TFR rail, first on the page and pinned under the masthead as on the reader (Ian, 2026-09-23). --}}
{{> "faith-received/_tfr-rail"}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Maps of the tradition | The Faith Received | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
<meta name="description" content="For every classic disputed question, the positions the tradition took, who holds each by tradition and century, and the lines between them." />
<link rel=preconnect href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel=preconnect href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel=stylesheet href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=EB+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&family=Source+Serif+Pro:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap">
<style>
.tfr-tool{--bg:var(--color-bg,#F0F0ED);--fg:var(--color-dark,#1C1C1A);--muted:var(--color-muted,#5A5A56);--border:var(--color-rule,#D8D8D3);--card-bg:var(--color-card,#FFFFFF);--highlight:var(--color-highlight,#E7E7E2);--accent:var(--color-accent,#8A3B2E);--grid:var(--color-rule,#E2E2DD);--refutes:#A8462B;--sel:var(--card-bg);--font-display:"EB Garamond",Georgia,serif;--font-body:"Source Serif Pro",Georgia,serif;--sans:var(--font-body,"Source Serif Pro",Georgia,serif);--ease:cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}
/* MAPS OF THE TRADITION (2026-10-21, owner: "conceptual diagrams, visualizations between the whole tradition"). v1/maps
   (runs/minimax_1019/maps/qmap.py): for each classic question the positions, who holds each (by tradition, placed in time), the
   relations between them, the axes and the turning points. The diagram is drawn here from the JSON; the lists below it carry the
   same on a phone and for a screen reader.
   ORGANIZED (2026-10-21, owner: "text like this as one block is a slop … organize apply design principles"): a position is its name and
   count, its thesis, what it turns on (a labelled note), then its holders by tradition, each tradition under the shelf colour the
   diagram uses, each holder one row (name and dates, his claim, the page at the right), six rows shown and the rest a click away.
   The atlas uses the same row. One type scale: secondary .8rem, body 1rem, headings 1.25 / 1.6 / 2rem.
   THE DESIGN PASS (2026-10-22, owner: "design is impeccable"): a position reads as one block from the top: its name and its share of
   the authors answering, a bar of that share in the traditions' colours with the traditions named under it, the thesis, what it
   turns on and its earliest holder, then its authors by tradition behind one fold (open when there are six or fewer); the legend is a
   legend (a tradition or a kind of line switched off goes hollow and grey), not a row of pills; a line that refutes is drawn in the
   one red the library gives refuting (--refutes: fr-reading-system.css, loaded after this sheet, makes --accent the ink, so the lines
   that refute had been drawn in ink like the rest); a chosen question is a sheet on the stone.
   THE FOLDS (2026-10-22, owner: "do a deep design UI and UX pass that makes the maps helpful, make this collapsable", the authors by
   tradition one after another, an endless scroll): the map comes first, drawn at the width it is shown (its labels at their true
   size, the column heads over their columns, each head opening its position), with its caption under it (the shape of the
   disagreement, what it runs along); then the positions as a list that folds, one open; in the open position its authors by
   tradition, a fold a tradition with its count, the tradition's count on the whole question, who they are and when; in an open
   tradition one line an author (name, dates, work, page) in order of birth, twelve and the rest behind Show all; an author opens in
   place, one at a time, to his claim in full, his answer, every page with its Preview and the lines between him and others. The
   lines between them fold by kind the same way, and their two ends open side by side. The question list keeps a line a question and
   one locus open; on a phone it folds behind "Choose a question", so the map comes first there too. Keys: up and down move through
   the rows, right opens, left closes; the address keeps the open position, tradition and author (#q002/p4/roman-catholic/
   alonso-tostado) and a bare #q002 still opens the question. The maps hold no passage in an author's own words: a row gives the
   reading of his page, not set as a quotation, and the page itself in its Preview (English, the source text or both); a map that
   ever carries his words (quote, or en and la) sets them as a quotation. */
.tfr-tool *{box-sizing:border-box}
.tfr-tool a{color:var(--fg)}
.tfr-tool :is(a,button,summary,input,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--fg);outline-offset:2px}
.tfr-tool :is(button,summary){touch-action:manipulation}
.tfr-tool .wrap{max-width:74rem;margin:0 auto;padding:1.8rem 1.2rem 4rem}
.tfr-tool h1{font:500 2rem/1.2 var(--font-display);margin:.2rem 0 .6rem;text-wrap:balance}
.tfr-tool .lede{max-width:66ch;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 1.4rem;text-wrap:pretty}
.tfr-tool .ct{color:var(--muted);font:400 .8rem/1.3 var(--sans);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
.tfr-tool .sr{position:absolute;left:-9999px}
.tfr-tool .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(15rem,19rem) minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;align-items:start}
.tfr-tool .nav{display:block;position:sticky;top:.8rem;max-height:calc(100vh - 1.6rem);overflow:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;padding:2px 2px 0}
.tfr-tool .find{width:100%;min-height:2.4rem;padding:.45rem .7rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;background:var(--card-bg);color:var(--fg);font:1rem var(--font-body);margin:0 0 .6rem}
.tfr-tool .find::placeholder{color:var(--muted)}
.tfr-tool .nav-t{display:none}
.tfr-tool .loci{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.tfr-tool .loci details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.tfr-tool .loci summary{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.5rem;min-height:2.5rem;padding:.55rem .2rem;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;font:500 1rem/1.3 var(--font-display)}
.tfr-tool .loci summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.tfr-tool .loci summary::before{content:"+";flex:none;width:.8rem;color:var(--muted);font:400 1rem/1.3 var(--sans);text-align:center}
.tfr-tool .loci details[open]>summary::before{content:"\2212"}
.tfr-tool .loci summary small{margin-left:auto;color:var(--muted);font:.8rem/1.3 var(--sans);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.tfr-tool .loci ul{list-style:none;margin:0 0 .5rem;padding:0}
.tfr-tool .loci li button{display:block;width:100%;min-height:2.25rem;padding:.4rem .6rem;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:none;color:var(--fg);font:1rem/1.4 var(--font-body);text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;cursor:pointer}
.tfr-tool .loci li button:hover{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border)}
.tfr-tool .loci li button[aria-current="true"]{white-space:normal;text-wrap:pretty;background:var(--sel);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border)}
.tfr-tool .loci li button small{display:none}
.tfr-tool .loci li button[aria-current="true"] small{display:block;margin-top:.1rem;color:var(--muted);font:.8rem/1.35 var(--sans)}
.tfr-tool .m h2{font:500 1.6rem/1.25 var(--font-display);margin:0 0 .3rem;text-wrap:balance}
.tfr-tool .meta{color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;margin:0 0 .9rem}
.tfr-tool .shape{max-width:72ch;margin:0 0 .8rem;text-wrap:pretty}
.tfr-tool .lab{display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content minmax(0,1fr);gap:.3rem 1.1rem;margin:0 0 1rem;max-width:76ch}
.tfr-tool .lab>div{display:contents}
.tfr-tool .lab dt{color:var(--muted);font:600 .8rem/1.95 var(--sans)}
